# Story page: moor
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Haunted Moor
---
The moor was grey, and the mist was grey, and the things in the mist were greyer still.

The ghosts did not care for walls. They came straight through them toward {name}, wailing, and touched it with fingers like a cold draught under a door.

{name} found that if it held its breath, it could go a little see-through itself. The ghosts found this very confusing. So did I. So, frankly, did {name}.
